{"id":"chatcmpl-9f3579e7-109f-409d-894a-43203c0c1a31","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229883,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates the importance of establishing spatial orientation before interpreting laterality-dependent findings in medical images. The successful strategy involved identifying orientation markers first, then systematically comparing bilateral structures to localize abnormalities. Verification through an expert tool confirmed the side-specific interpretation, showing how explicit orientation reasoning prevents left-right confusion errors.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When interpreting images with laterality-dependent findings, first identify and interpret any orientation markers or labels before assessing the finding itself.\",\n    \"For bilateral comparison tasks, systematically inspect both sides and describe the normal side as a reference before characterizing the abnormal side.\",\n    \"When visual evidence suggests a side-specific finding, explicitly state the orientation reasoning (marker interpretation) to justify the laterality conclusion.\",\n    \"Use domain-specific verification tools to confirm interpretations that depend on correct spatial orientation, especially when markers could be ambiguous.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Always establish image orientation (markers, labels, standard conventions) before localizing findings; compare bilateral structures systematically.\",\n    \"Visual comparison tasks\": \"Describe the normal/reference side first, then contrast with the abnormal side to make the finding salient and verifiable.\",\n    \"Ambiguous spatial reasoning\": \"Explicitly articulate the mapping between image coordinates and real-world/anatomical sides, then use that mapping consistently in the final answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm orientation markers/labels and state the image-to-anatomy side mapping before concluding laterality.\",\n    \"Verify the side-specific finding against a reference (normal contralateral side or expert tool) before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":564,"total_tokens":905,"completion_tokens":341,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":564},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":341}}}